<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" data-marble="1">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
<meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">
<meta name="mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">
<meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-title" content="Projects">
<!-- Projects: the drive's work grouped by what it is for. This file holds
     only what the owner says about their work: each project's name, its one
     sentence, how much it matters, its dates and what it lives in. Everything
     that can be counted (chats, what is running, which weeks were busy) is
     read live from the host, and the views are drawn around these elements by
     runtime/projects.js and runtime/projects.css, which the host injects here
     so they ship with every release instead of being merged into this file.
     Design: Notes and Sketches/App Designs/Projects design. -->
<meta name="marble-projects" content="1">
<title>__TITLE__</title>
__ICON__
<style>
  /* Only what the page must be before its own sheet arrives: the paper, in
     both schemes, so the first frame is not a white flash. */
  :root { color-scheme: light dark; }
  html, body { margin: 0; background: light-dark(#fafaf7, #16181a); }
</style>
</head>
<body data-marble-id="__ID__">
<main data-marble-id="__ID__" data-projects data-view="gallery" data-sort="ranked" data-zoom="quarter">
  <div data-marble-id="prj-list" class="prj-list"></div>
  <ul data-marble-id="prj-declined" class="prj-declined"></ul>
  <p data-marble-id="prj-runline" class="prj-run">
    <button data-marble-id="prj-run" type="button" data-marble-run="Bring the projects in this list up to date. Each project is an article.project; its members (ul.p-members) name the folders and documents it lives in (data-kind and data-path), the code checkouts it uses (data-kind=&quot;code&quot;, data-runs-in) and chats filed in it by hand (data-chat). The drive's chats are in .marble/agents/*/meta.json, each with a target document, a project (where it ran), a title and times. For each project that had chats or edits since yesterday: rewrite its p.p-sentence as one plain sentence of under twenty words saying what the work is doing now, unless that sentence has data-by=&quot;you&quot;. Then, at most twice per project, when a folder or document clearly belongs to it and is in no project yet, add a suggestion as an li in its ol.p-suggest with data-kind (doc or folder), data-path, and a short reason as its text, unless its kind:path is a data-key in ul.prj-declined. Change nothing else." data-marble-scope="prj-list" data-marble-on="daily 07:00">Update now</button>
    <button data-marble-id="prj-pause" type="button" data-marble-pause="prj-run">Pause</button>
  </p>
</main>
</body>
</html>
